olspan="1">1436 &#x000b1; 71</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">28 &#x000b1; 26</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">2195 &#x000b1; 57</td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">23 &#x000b1; 3</td></tr></tbody></table><table-wrap-foot><fn id="TF3"><p><sup>a</sup>The final 200 structures were clustered based on the pair-wise RMSD matrix using a 1.0 &#x000c5; cutoff. The statistics are for the 10 lowest energy structures.</p></fn><fn id="TF4"><p><sup>b</sup>The HADDOCK score was calculated as the sum of: <italic>E</italic><sub>vdw</sub> + <italic>E</italic><sub>elec</sub> + <italic>E</italic><sub>AIR</sub> + <italic>E</italic><sub>sani</sub> + <italic>E</italic><sub>desolv</sub>.</p></fn><fn id="TF5"><p><sup>c</sup>Overall backbone RMSD from the lowest energy structure.</p></fn><fn id="TF6"><p><sup>d</sup>Number of structures in a given cluster.</p></fn><fn id="TF7"><p><sup>e</sup>Intermolecular energies (kcal mol<sup>&#x02212;1</sup>) were calculated with the OPLS parameters using a 8.5 &#x000c5; cut-off.</p></fn><fn id="TF8"><p><sup>f</sup>HADDOCK ambiguous interaction restraint energy (kcal mol<sup>&#x02212;1</sup>).</p></fn><fn id="TF9"><p><sup>g</sup>Energy for the direct RDC constraints.</p></fn><fn id="TF10"><p><sup>h</sup>Buried surface area (&#x000c5;<sup>2</sup>).</p></fn><fn id="TF11"><p><sup>i</sup>The desolvation energy (kcal mol<sup>&#x02212;1</sup>).</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap><table-wrap id="T3" position="float"><label>Table 3.</label><caption><p>Intermolecular hydrogen bonds between <italic>tv</italic>Myb1<sub>35&#x02013;141</sub> and DNA</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups"><thead align="left"><tr><th rowspan="1" colspan="1">Protein</th><th rowspan="1" colspan="1">Atom</th><th rowspan="1" colspan="1">Base</th><th rowspan="1" colspan="1">Atom</th><th rowspan="1" colspan="1">Distance (&#x000c5;)</th><th rowspan="1" colspan="1">No. (of 10)</th></tr></thead><tbody align="left"><tr><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">Hydrogen bonds</td><td rowspan="1" colsp